What draws you to this, and what preparation you already have for it.

Two things to keep out: a timeline, and the word "will". This is an intention held
provisionally, not a commitment to whoever is reading. Present tense of attention —
what you are drawn toward — rather than future tense of promise.

One thing to keep in: the honest version of why it is yours to attempt. "This field
is important and I am interested in it" is positioning. Something you were prepared
for without arranging it is not.
